# HANDOFF: Board Game Prototype Sandbox

This folder is a no-build, static prototype for experimenting with: generate a topographic map, paint terrain (forest/river), spawn pieces, and play with turn-based movement/rotation/attacks using morale.

## Run

- Static: `python3 -m http.server 8000` then `http://localhost:8000/`
- With spreadsheet auto-save: `python3 dev-server.py` then `http://localhost:8000/`
  - Server endpoints:
    - `GET /api/damage-matrix` loads `damage-matrix.md`
    - `POST /api/damage-matrix` overwrites `damage-matrix.md`

## UI Overview

- **Stage**: 3-column layout (left: map settings, center: canvas, right: selected unit).
- **Top toolbar**: piece spawn palette + turn indicator + `End Turn`.
- **Below stage**: Log, then the “Attack Damage Matrix” spreadsheet.

## Current Rules Implemented

- Map generation:
  - Perlin-noise heightmap, quantized to 10-level elevation bands.
  - Green palette; contour lines are black.
  - Seed is randomized per `Start`.
- Painting (before finalizing):
  - `Forest` and `River` paint onto an overlay, and also write into a terrain grid used by attack modifiers.
  - `Finalize Map` hides map settings and disables painting.
- Pieces:
  - Pieces are rectangles (Infantry/Cavalry) or squares (Artillery), with per-type markings.
  - Spawn buttons create pieces at random positions on the map.
  - Morale is the “health” mechanic; when morale reaches 0 the unit becomes “broken” (white) and can’t move/attack.
- Turns:
  - `End Turn` toggles Red/Blue and resets per-turn actions for the active team.
  - At turn start, each active-team unit regains `+1` morale (capped at max).
- Movement:
  - All units can move once per turn within their movement radius (drag to reposition).
  - The movement circle stays anchored to the unit’s start-of-turn position.
- Rotation:
  - Hold `Ctrl` and drag to rotate (once per turn).
- Attacks:
  - Right-click an enemy unit to attack (once per turn).
  - Attacks only apply within the unit’s front 90° arc and within melee/ranged radius.
  - Hovering an enemy shows expected morale damage + modifier breakdown.
  - Damage uses the editable 3×3 “Attack Damage Matrix” (split per defender into ranged/melee columns).

## Key Files

- `index.html`: UI structure (controls, tool palettes, status).
- `styles.css`: layout and visual styles.
- `simulation.js`: map generator, paint overlay, pieces, turns, movement/rotation/attacks, tooltip, spreadsheet wiring.
- `damage-matrix.md`: persisted spreadsheet values when running `dev-server.py`.
- `update_damage_matrix_md.py`: script that writes `damage-matrix.md` from the in-browser editor.
- `dev-server.py`: minimal local server that can save the spreadsheet to disk.

## Known Caveats

- 1024×1024 generation can be slow on some machines; generation yields to keep the UI responsive.
- If you run the page without `dev-server.py`, the spreadsheet persists in `localStorage`, but it cannot auto-write to `damage-matrix.md`.
